# The two transfer icons, stored as BITMASKS rather than as PNGs the way
# the logo is. Two reasons. They are pixel art, so one bit per cell is all
# the information there is - about 500 bytes each, against ~9 KB apiece as
# PNGs. And a stored PNG carries fixed colours: the artwork is white on
# black, which would sit as a black square on every panel and disappear
# entirely on "latte" and "bright". Rendered from a mask, each takes the
# theme's colour and a transparent background.
#
# (width, height, mask) with the mask packed row-major, one bit per cell,
# each row padded to a byte boundary. The two differ by two rows: they were
# drawn separately, and forcing them onto one grid would have cost a row of
# the device's pads.
